{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1779809616,"nonce":"khB+qm2yIqGtILJY98eZPo5qakM=","metadata":{"github-id":"UCE_lAHOK4fCvM8AAAABDVF0786-bHvA"},"target":"20a49fcd9bd6820a06b2b4edc822b4ce59fc9283caa7f0c9406214e4d1805dca","message":"## Next BizzyBoat deployment\n\n\u003e **Set the date** in the title when scheduled (convention: `Deployment YYYY-MM-DD: …`). Created ahead of time to carry validation reminders for the turning-limit changes from [#124](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/124) §2.\n\n## ⚠️ Validate changed turning limits\n\nTwo limits changed since the last deployment — **both are field-untested**. Check how they affect the boat:\n\n### 1. Helm yaw cap raised 0.5 → 1.0 rad/s\n`helm_manager.max_yaw_speed` ([PR #172](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/pull/172), #124 §2). Now the vehicle-capability backstop (~1.5 m turn radius at cruise).\n- [ ] GUIDED cruise turns track the higher command **without oscillation / overshoot**.\n- [ ] **Steering-direction consistency** holds at the higher yaw rate (the stationary controls-check reversal is a known artifact — confirm it doesn't appear on-water).\n- [ ] Note line-transition sharpness and any heel/wake that could disturb the sonar.\n\n### 2. Planner min turning radius reduced 3.0 → 1.5 m\n`SmacPlannerHybrid.minimum_turning_radius` (shared Nav2 config; [seafloor_echoboat_project11#24](https://github.com/rolker/seafloor_echoboat_project11/pull/24)). Also affects the seafloor EchoBoat.\n- [ ] Planned **line-transitions are tighter (~1.5 m)** as expected; no planning failures / degraded path quality.\n- [ ] **Sonar settling** on the new line after the tighter turn is acceptable for survey data.\n\n### Context to keep in mind\n- The cmd_vel filter chain (velocity_smoother + other filters) remains **deliberately disconnected** (from earlier troubleshooting) — so the helm clamp is the sole cmd_vel governor and the **planner radius is currently the only turn-gentleness control**. Confirm this is still the intended state for the deployment.\n- If line-transitions are too sharp for the sonar, the knob is the planner radius (raise it) and/or re-enabling the smoother with a survey yaw limit — not the helm cap.\n\n## 📋 Land before deployment: log `pid_state` (cross-track error)\n\nEnable bag recording of the CrabbingPathFollower's PID state, so the next mission captures **cross-track error + controller internals** (`control_msgs/PidState`: `error`=XTE, p/i/d terms, `output`=crab command). This is the missing data that would settle [#164](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/164) (SE-line undulation — high-gain limit-cycling vs. a disturbance the gains can't reject). The state publisher is **already live** (`activate_state_publisher: true` in the shared Nav2 config); it's just not in the recording list.\n\n- [ ] **Verify the exact topic name on the running stack** — do *not* guess; a wrong name silently records nothing (the same silent-failure class as #171/#162). On gabby with the nav stack up: `ros2 topic list | grep -i pid`. *(Source note: the follower builds `PidROS` with `topic_prefix=\"FollowPath/pid\"` — starts with an alphanumeric, so per control_toolbox `pid_ros.hpp` the topic is in the **global** namespace, i.e. ~`/FollowPath/pid/pid_state`, **not** under `/bizzy`. Confirm the precise string before editing.)*\n- [ ] Add the confirmed topic to the `/**/logger` → `record:` → `topics:` list in `bizzyboat_project11/config/bizzyboat.yaml` (full path + one-line comment, matching the existing entries). Via issue → worktree → PR.\n- [ ] **In-deployment check:** once recording starts, confirm `pid_state` is actually present in the bag (`ros2 bag info`) — don't repeat the \"published-but-not-recorded\" gap.\n\n## 🔧 During deployment (opportunistic): operator annunciator coverage (#171)\n\nAdd **battery**, **FCU-system**, and **sound-speed** indicators to the operator annunciator (today it has only network/link rows), so the operator actually gets these warnings — gaps surfaced by the 2026-05-22 drain-to-LVD test ([#171](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/171)). Self-contained below so it works without GitHub access in the field (provenance / detail: [PR #180](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/pull/180)). Best done live since the rows key on exact diagnostic strings.\n\n**1. Confirm exact strings on the live bus** (operator station, stack up) — don't guess; a wrong string silently matches nothing (same class as the `pid_state` task above):\n```bash\nros2 topic list | grep -i -E 'battery|diagnostic'\nros2 topic echo /diagnostics --once     # exact DiagnosticStatus.name + KeyValue keys\n```\n- [ ] `mavros: Battery` → exact **Voltage** KeyValue casing (on mismatch the row fails loud as `Voltage?`/ERROR, not silent green)\n- [ ] `mavros: System` status name (carries \"Battery N is low\" + FCU ERRORs; `mavros: Heartbeat` is already the boat \"FCU\" row)\n- [ ] the exact name `sound_speed_bridge` publishes — and that it publishes one at all (see #163); use `match_mode: substring` if it has a host/instance suffix\n- [ ] op-side **republished** name of `/bizzy/mavros/battery` — only needed for the topic-source battery fallback (step 3)\n\n**2. Append to `bizzyboat_project11/config/bizzyboat_operator_annunciator.yaml`:**\n```yaml\n  # --- Boat health (forwarded over the link) ---\n  - name: Battery            # battery mechanism: see step 3\n    source: diagnostics\n    diagnostic_name: \"mavros: Battery\"\n    value_key: Voltage       # confirm casing live\n    format: \"{:.2f} V\"\n    thresholds:\n      warn: \"value \u003c 23.0\"   # FCU BATT_LOW_VOLT; tune vs Torqeedo Power 24-3500\n      error: \"value \u003c 21.5\"  # FCU BATT_CRT_VOLT\n  - name: FCU System\n    source: diagnostics\n    diagnostic_name: \"mavros: System\"\n    format: \"{}\"\n  - name: Sound Speed\n    source: diagnostics\n    diagnostic_name: \"sound_speed_bridge\"\n    match_mode: substring\n    format: \"{}\"\n    stale_timeout: 10.0\n```\n- [ ] Add the same `Sound Speed` row to `bizzyboat_annunciator.yaml` (boat side) — mind the overlap with [#179](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/pull/179)'s battery-row edit (different rows, just merge-order).\n\n**3. Battery indicator — pick by what's deployed:**\n- If [rqt_operator_tools#36](https://github.com/rolker/rqt_operator_tools/pull/36) is deployed to the op station → use the `source: diagnostics` block above (consistent with the boat-side #162/#179 fix).\n- If **not** → fallback that works on the *current* engine (topic-source on the forwarded BatteryState):\n```yaml\n  - name: Battery\n    source: topic\n    topic: \u003cop-side republished /bizzy/mavros/battery\u003e   # confirm live (step 1)\n    msg_type: sensor_msgs/msg/BatteryState\n    value_field: voltage\n    format: \"{:.2f} V\"\n    thresholds:\n      warn: \"value \u003c 23.0\"\n      error: \"value \u003c 21.5\"\n```\nFCU-System and Sound-Speed have **no** #36 dependency either way.\n\n**4. Land it.** If the op-station checkout is gitcloud-origin → edit/commit/push in field mode, reconcile via `/import-field-changes` post-deployment. If GitHub-origin → normal worktree/PR.\n- [ ] Threshold values 23.0 / 21.5 (FCU params) — tune vs pack behavior if needed.\n\n## 📁 Logs\n\n- **dev** — [`docs/logs/2026/2026-05-26_dev_logs.md`](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/blob/feature/issue-173/docs/logs/2026/2026-05-26_dev_logs.md) (on `feature/issue-173`)\n- **gabby / salmon / mercat** — added as field logs appear (pushed to gitcloud, reconciled at wrap-up)\n- **Wrap-up PR**: [#182](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/pull/182) (draft) — `Closes #173`\n\n## 🎯 Stretch goals (only if the boat day allows)\n\nPer the roadmap's \"boat days are serial — combine them\" guidance. The core scope above (turning limits, `pid_state`, reflex collision avoidance, annunciator verify) comes first; pull these in only if there's time:\n\n- [ ] [#138](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/138) — **in-water** validation of the FCU / tide chain. FCU param applied (`f348f66`) + bench-validated; the trackline/sea-surface validation never ran on water.\n- [ ] [#130](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/130) — OTH Starlink-only operation with a **completed survey** (the still-open must-finish OTH criterion).\n- [ ] [unh_marine_navigation#23](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_navigation/issues/23) — confirm TF-extrapolation errors on multi-line survey goals (verify-in-deployment).\n- [ ] [unh_marine_navigation#19](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_navigation/issues/19) — costmap-update-timeout (1.0s) under realistic load.\n- [ ] [perception#7](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_perception/issues/7) OAK→costmap + [autonomy#127](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_autonomy/issues/127) op-side costmap display — if ready, check the bandwidth fit.\n- [ ] Topic-budget cull measurement + VPN-path indicator ([#124](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/124)) under OTH load.\n\n## Standard deployment\n- [ ] Pre-deployment checklist (per the usual convention)\n- [ ] Per-host logs at `docs/logs/YYYY/YYYY-MM-DD_\u003chost\u003e_logs.md`\n- [ ] Wrap-up PR (`Closes #\u003cthis\u003e`)\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":4,"timestamp":1779846531,"nonce":"pbPBjD2BVvKPSvDAiGWb3gsOTcM=","metadata":{"github-id":"CE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABDVF0788AAAAGDWGWVQ"},"status":2}]}